@title Disaster Recovery Drill, 2026-10-07
@subtitle Bramble Health Platform Resilience runbook and results

# Scope

We simulated the loss of us-west-2 and restored the patient-scheduling service in us-east-2 from backups.

# Restore procedure

1. Freeze writes in us-west-2.
2. Restore the latest RDS snapshot in us-east-2.
3. Restore the S3 attachments bucket from the replica.
4. Deploy the service stack from the release tag.

!! Confirm the snapshot timestamp first. Promoting an old snapshot silently loses appointments.

5. Switch DNS for scheduling.bramble.example to us-east-2.
6. Run the smoke test suite.
7. Reopen writes.

# Results

table = Metric,Target,Achieved; RTO,60 minutes,74 minutes; RPO,15 minutes,9 minutes; Smoke tests passed,48 of 48,46 of 48; Data verified,100 percent,100 percent

data phases = phase,minutes; Snapshot restore,31; S3 restore,12; Stack deploy,18; DNS switch,6; Smoke tests,7

chart bar phases y=minutes labels unit=min title="Minutes spent per phase"

# Follow-ups

- Pre-provision the database subnet group in us-east-2 to cut restore time.
- Fix the 2 smoke tests that depend on a us-west-2-only endpoint.
- Next drill on 2027-01-13.
